{"tool_name":"hicplotter","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"hicplotter","home":"https://github.com/kcakdemir/HiCPlotter","summary":"Python data visualization tool for integrating different data types with interaction matrixes.","addition_date":"2017-08-03T18:46:28Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:22:18.755773Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:hicplotter","credit":[{"email":"kcakedemir@mdanderson.org","name":"Kadir Akdemir","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://twitter.com/canerakdemir"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/kcakdemir/HiCPlotter/blob/master/README.md"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}]}],"maturity":"Emerging","name":"HiCPlotter Beta","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"mbs_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-015-0767-1","metadata":{"abstract":"Metazoan genomic material is folded into stable non-randomly arranged chromosomal structures that are tightly associated with transcriptional regulation and DNA replication. Various factors including regulators of pluripotency, long non-coding RNAs, or the presence of architectural proteins have been implicated in regulation and assembly of the chromatin architecture. Therefore, comprehensive visualization of this multi-faceted structure is important to unravel the connections between nuclear architecture and transcriptional regulation. Here, we present an easy-to-use open-source visualization tool, HiCPlotter, to facilitate juxtaposition of Hi-C matrices with diverse genomic assay outputs, as well as to compare interaction matrices between various conditions.","authors":[{"name":"Akdemir K.C."},{"name":"Chin L."}],"citationCount":140,"date":"2015-09-21T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genome Biology","title":"HiCPlotter integrates genomic data with interaction